 38		\leanok
 39		If $a=0$, then $\tr[\bx\cdot a]=0$ for every $\bx$, so the average is $1$. If $a\neq 0$, choose $y \in \F_q$ such that $\tr[a\cdot y]\neq 0$, and set
 40		\[
 41			C=\E_{\bx \sim \F_q} \omega^{\tr[\bx \cdot a]}.
 42		\]
 43		Translation invariance of the uniform distribution gives
 44		\[
 45			C=\E_{\bx \sim \F_q} \omega^{\tr[(\bx+y)\cdot a]}
 46			= C \cdot \omega^{\tr[y\cdot a]}.
 47		\]
 48		Since $\omega^{\tr[y\cdot a]}\neq 1$, it follows that $C=0$.
 49	\end{proof}
